 peptidoglycan.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>280</volume><fpage>326</fpage><lpage>333</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15522883</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000500-Meylan1"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meylan</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Tschopp</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The RIP kinases: crucial integrators of cellular stress.</article-title><source>Trends Biochem Sci</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>151</fpage><lpage>159</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15752987</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000500-Ogura1"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ogura</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Inohara</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Benito</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>FF</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamaoka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Nod2, a Nod1/Apaf-1 family member that is restricted to monocytes and activates NF-kappaB.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>276</volume><fpage>4812</fpage><lpage>4818</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11087742</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000500-McCarthy1"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCarthy</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name><name><surname>Ni</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dixit</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>RIP2 is a novel NF-kappaB-activating and cell death-inducing kinase.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>273</